# 3. THE JOURNAL

The player should have a personal journal that can be opened at any time by pressing J.

This should be a fully interactive journal where the player can actually write their own entries.

### Journal features
- Allow the player to type whatever they want.
- Allow entries to be saved.
- Display previous entries in chronological order.
- Show the date and time when each entry was written.
- Allow entries to be edited and deleted.
- Give the journal an attractive old-fashioned nautical appearance.
- Include a realistic paper background, ink-style text and page-turning animations if possible.

Automatically create journal entries for important events, such as:
- Discovering a shipwreck.
- Finding gold.
- Trading with a merchant.
- Rescuing survivors.
- Surviving a storm.
- Winning or losing a pirate battle.
- Discovering a new area.
- Expanding the boat.
- Losing crew members.

Automatic entries should not prevent the player from writing their own entries.

All journal entries must be saved between game sessions.

