# 11. SHIP DAMAGE AND REPAIR SYSTEM

Ships should have individual damage systems.

Different parts of the ship should be able to take damage.

Include:
- Hull damage.
- Sail damage.
- Mast damage.
- Steering damage.
- Cannon damage.
- Deck damage.

Display the ship's condition in the ship management menu.

### Damage effects

Damage must actually affect gameplay.

Examples:
- Hull damage causes water to enter the boat.
- Severe leaks slowly flood the ship.
- Damaged sails reduce movement speed.
- Broken masts reduce sailing effectiveness.
- Damaged steering makes turning difficult.
- Destroyed cannons cannot fire.
- Damaged sections may require several crew members to repair.

### Repairs

Allow crew members to repair the boat using wood, rope, iron and other materials.

The player should choose which sections to repair first.

Repairs should take time.

During storms or battles, repairing the ship should be harder.

Merchant ships should also be able to sell repair materials and equipment.

